<title>AUSTRALIA: RTRS-FORECAST-Australia Q3 GDP seen up 0.9 pct.</title>
<headline>RTRS-FORECAST-Australia Q3 GDP seen up 0.9 pct.</headline>
<dateline>SYDNEY 1996-12-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>The following are results of a Reuter survey of economists on Australian GDP forecasts for the September quarter (s/adj). Comparison with previous quarter unless stated. GDP figures are due out at 0030 GMT on Wednesday.</p>
<p>Figures have been revised following stocks data on Monday.</p>
<p>				  Median Forecasts     Prev Actual</p>
<p>    Gross Domestic Product  Sept qtr	     June qtr</p>
<p>    GDP-Average		 +0.9 pct	     +0.1 pct</p>
<p>    GDP-Income based	  +0.8 pct	     +0.3 pct</p>
<p>    GDP-Expenditure based   +1.2 pct	     +0.2 pct</p>
<p>    GDP-Production based   +0.75 pct	     -0.2 pct</p>
<p>CS 1st Boston     +0.9   +0.3   +1.8   +0.7   +1.2    3.5</p>
<p>County NatWest    +0.6    n/a    n/a    n/a    n/a    3.1</p>
<p>Deutche MG	  +1.2   +1.0   +1.8   +0.9   +0.9    3.7</p>
<p>GIO Australia     +0.9   +0.9   +1.2   +0/7    n/a    3.4</p>
<p>James Capel	 +0.7   +0.2   +1.6   +0.5   +1.2    3.1</p>
<p>JB Were	     +0.9   +0.8   +1.2   +0.8   +0.9    3.4</p>
<p>Macquarie	 +1.0/1.2 +1.2   +1.2   +1.0   +0.8    3.6</p>
<p>McIntosh	    +0.9   +0.5   +1.7   +0.6   +0.9    3.4</p>
<p>Merril Lynch	+1.0   +0.9   +1.4   +0.9   +0.7    3.5</p>
<p>Nomura		+0.7   +0.4   +1.3   +0.2   +1.0    3.1</p>
<p>PruBache	    +1.0   +0.7   +0.8   +1.8   +1.1    3.5</p>
<p>Rothschild	  +1.0    n/a    n/a    n/a    n/a    3.4</p>
<p>SBC Warburg	 +1.1   +0.5   +1.9   +0.8   +1.7    3.5</p>
<p>Schroders	   +0.7    n/a    n/a    n/a    n/a    3.1</p>
